{"term":"hectic","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7bc9ce605aa2c9d084","definition":"Very busy with activity and confusion.","example":"The city center is so hectic at 8 in the morning that I go to work an hour beforehand to avoid the crowds","pos":"adj","synonyms":["feverish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["antihectic","hectically","hecticity","hecticness","hectivity","unhectic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hectic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0594ebe2dd187641b0","definition":"Denoting a type of fever accompanying consumption and similar wasting diseases, characterised by flushed cheeks and dry skin.","example":"hectic fever","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["antihectic","hectically","hecticity","hecticness","hectivity","unhectic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hectic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ce9720db8a4e2b9733","definition":"Pertaining to or symptomatic of such a fever.","example":"Ann had a hectic cough, and many unfavourable prognostics […].","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["antihectic","hectically","hecticity","hecticness","hectivity","unhectic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hectic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e036529d967cee74a","definition":"A hectic fever.","example":"[…] Do it England, / For like the Hecticke in my blood he rages, / And thou muſt cure me: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFa